# Configuration control and process verification templates (FI 5 aerospace pack).

block config_header
section config_identification | Configuration item | 3
f cf_item | Configuration item | text | *
f cf_part | Part | part
f cf_baseline | Baseline | choice | [Functional; Allocated; Product; Other]
f cf_program | Program or contract | text
f cf_customer_approval | Customer approval required | boolean
f cf_owner | Configuration manager | user | *
end

block config_signatures
sign cf_prepared | Prepared by | prepared | I prepared this configuration record.
sign cf_reviewed | Reviewed by | reviewed | I reviewed this configuration record.
sign cf_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve this configuration record. | changes.approve
end

block pv_header
section pv_identification | Process | 3
f pv_process | Process | text | *
f pv_kind | Process kind | choice | * [Special process; Heat treatment; Welding; Brazing; Plating and coating; Chemical processing; Non-destructive testing; Bonding; Machining; Assembly; Other]
f pv_spec | Process specification | record | *
f pv_spec_rev | Specification revision | text | *
f pv_equipment | Equipment | equipment
f pv_operator | Operator | user
end

block pv_signatures
sign pv_performed | Performed by | performed | I performed this verification as recorded.
sign pv_verified | Verified by | verified | I verified the results against the process specification.
sign pv_approved | Quality approval | approved | I approve this process verification. | inspection.approve
end

template configuration-item-register | Configuration Item Register | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags configuration control, configuration items, baseline
purpose List the items under configuration control with their current approved configuration, baseline and effectivity, so the configuration of any delivered product can be established.
scope Products, assemblies, software and documents the organization or its customer places under configuration control.
instructions Add each configuration item with its identifier, current revision and effectivity. Items with open changes are highlighted.
workflow Maintained by the configuration manager, updated by each approved change, reviewed at configuration audits.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the period required by contract.
section cir_scope | Register | 3
f cir_program | Program or contract | text
f cir_owner | Configuration manager | user | *
f cir_as_of | As of | date | *
section cir_items | Items | 1
landscape-section
table cir_rows | Configuration items | 1
groups Item:3; Configuration:3; Status:2
c ci_id | Identifier | text | *
c ci_name | Name | text | *
c ci_type | Type | choice | * [Hardware; Software; Firmware; Document; Interface]
c ci_rev | Current revision | text | *
c ci_baseline | Baseline | choice | [Functional; Allocated; Product; Other]
c ci_effectivity | Effectivity | text
c ci_open_changes | Open changes | integer | min=0
c ci_status | Status | choice | [Active; Under change; Superseded; Retired]
rule cir_rows.ci_open_changes | greaterThan | 0 | #FFF4D6 | bold
rule cir_rows.ci_status | equals | Superseded | #EEF2F7
f cir_count | Items | calc | {COUNTA(cir_rows.ci_id)}
f cir_with_changes | Items with open changes | calc | {COUNTIF(cir_rows.ci_open_changes, ">0")}
use config_signatures
end

template configuration-change-record | Configuration Change Record | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags configuration control, change, effectivity
purpose Propose, classify, evaluate and approve a change to a configuration item, and record its effectivity and the documents it revises.
scope Changes to items under configuration control.
instructions Classify the change. A change that affects form, fit, function, safety, reliability or interchangeability is major and needs the approvals the contract requires. Record every document revised and the effectivity.
workflow Proposed, classified, evaluated, approved by the configuration control board, implemented, verified.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the period required by contract.
use config_header
section ccr_change | Change | 2
f ccr_description | Description of the change | longtext | *
f ccr_reason | Reason | longtext | *
f ccr_form | Affects form | boolean
f ccr_fit | Affects fit | boolean
f ccr_function | Affects function | boolean
f ccr_safety | Affects safety or reliability | boolean
f ccr_interchange | Affects interchangeability | boolean
f ccr_class | Classification | calc | {IF(COUNTIF(CELLS(ccr_form, ccr_fit, ccr_function, ccr_safety, ccr_interchange), TRUE) > 0, "Major", "Minor")}
rule ccr_class | equals | Major | #FDE7E9 | bold
section ccr_docs | Documents revised | 1
table ccr_doc_rows | Documents | 1
c cd_document | Document | record
c cd_number | Number | text | *
c cd_from | From revision | text | *
c cd_to | To revision | text | *
section ccr_effectivity | Effectivity | 2
f ccr_effectivity_type | Effectivity by | choice | * [Serial number; Lot; Date; Contract; Next order]
f ccr_effectivity | Effectivity | text | *
f ccr_stock | Disposition of existing stock | choice | [Use as is; Rework; Scrap; Return to supplier; Not applicable]
f ccr_wip | Disposition of work in progress | choice | [Use as is; Rework; Scrap; Not applicable]
section ccr_board | Configuration control board | 2
f ccr_board_date | Board date | date
f ccr_board_decision | Decision | choice | [Approved; Approved with conditions; Rejected; Deferred]
f ccr_customer_ref | Customer approval reference | text | reqwhen=cf_customer_approval=true
f ccr_verified | Implementation verified | boolean
rule ccr_board_decision | equals | Rejected | #FDE7E9 | bold
sign ccr_prepared | Proposed by | prepared | I propose this change and the information in it is complete.
sign ccr_reviewed | Configuration manager | reviewed | I classified and reviewed this change.
sign ccr_approved | Board approval | approved | I approve this change for implementation. | changes.approve
sign ccr_customer | Customer approval | customer | The customer approves this change. | | optional
end

template configuration-status-accounting | Configuration Status Accounting Report | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags configuration control, status accounting
purpose Report the approved configuration of a product and the status of every proposed and approved change, so the as-designed and as-built configuration can be compared.
scope One product or configuration item at a stated date.
instructions List the changes with their status and incorporation. Changes approved but not yet incorporated in the serials reported are counted.
workflow Compiled by the configuration manager, reviewed, issued.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the period required by contract.
use config_header
section csa_period | Report | 2
f csa_as_of | As of | date | *
f csa_serials | Serial numbers covered | text
section csa_changes | Changes | 1
table csa_rows | Changes | 1
c cs_change | Change | record
c cs_number | Change number | text | *
c cs_class | Class | choice | [Major; Minor]
c cs_status | Status | choice | * [Proposed; Approved; Rejected; Incorporated]
c cs_effectivity | Effectivity | text
c cs_incorporated | Incorporated in serials reported | boolean
rule csa_rows.cs_status | equals | Approved | #FFF4D6
f csa_pending | Approved, not incorporated | calc | {COUNTIF(csa_rows.cs_status, "Approved")}
f csa_proposed | Proposed | calc | {COUNTIF(csa_rows.cs_status, "Proposed")}
use config_signatures
end

template configuration-audit | Configuration Audit | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags configuration control, functional audit, physical audit
purpose Verify that a configuration item meets its requirements (functional) and that the as-built item matches its approved documentation (physical).
scope Configuration items at the baselines the contract or the organization requires.
instructions Check each requirement or drawing feature against the evidence. Discrepancies become findings with actions.
workflow Planned, performed, reported, findings closed, approved.
retention Keep for the life of the product plus the period required by contract.
use config_header
section ca_scope | Audit | 3
f ca_type | Audit type | choice | * [Functional configuration audit; Physical configuration audit; Combined]
f ca_serial | Serial number audited | text
f ca_date | Date | date | *
section ca_checks | Checks | 1
table ca_rows | Checks | 1
c cak_item | Requirement or feature | text | *
c cak_reference | Document and revision | text | *
c cak_evidence | Evidence | text
c cak_result | Result | passfail | *
c cak_finding | Finding | text
rule ca_rows.cak_result | equals | fail | #FDE7E9 | bold
f ca_discrepancies | Discrepancies | calc | {COUNTIF(ca_rows.cak_result, "fail")}
f ca_conclusion | Conclusion | choice | * [Configuration confirmed; Confirmed with findings; Not confirmed]
use config_signatures
end

template process-verification-record | Process Verification Record | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags process verification, special process
purpose Verify that a process run met its specification: the parameters actually used against their limits, the operator and equipment qualifications and the results of any test pieces.
scope Processes whose results need verification against a process specification, including special processes.
instructions Record each parameter as actually run. Values outside the limits are highlighted and counted. Confirm the operator and equipment qualifications before release.
workflow Performed, verified, approved by quality.
retention Keep with the product record for the period the contract or regulation requires.
use pv_header
section pvr_run | Run | 3
f pvr_job | Job or lot | text | *
f pvr_part | Part | part
f pvr_quantity | Quantity | integer | min=0
f pvr_date | Date | date | *
f pvr_operator_qualified | Operator qualification current | boolean | *
f pvr_equipment_qualified | Equipment qualification and calibration current | boolean | *
section pvr_parameters | Parameters | 1
table pvr_param_rows | Parameters as run | 1
c pp_parameter | Parameter | text | *
c pp_unit | Unit | text
c pp_low | Lower limit | number | * dec=3
c pp_high | Upper limit | number | * dec=3
c pp_actual | Actual | number | * dec=3
c pp_in_limits | In limits | calc | {IF(AND(pp_actual >= pp_low, pp_actual <= pp_high), "Yes", "No")}
rule pvr_param_rows.pp_in_limits | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
f pvr_out | Parameters out of limits | calc | {COUNTIF(pvr_param_rows.pp_in_limits, "No")}
section pvr_tests | Test pieces | 1
table pvr_test_rows | Test pieces | 0
c pt_test | Test | text | *
c pt_requirement | Requirement | text
c pt_result | Result | text
c pt_outcome | Outcome | passfail | *
rule pvr_test_rows.pt_outcome | equals | fail | #FDE7E9 | bold
f pvr_tests_failed | Test pieces failed | calc | {COUNTIF(pvr_test_rows.pt_outcome, "fail")}
section pvr_decision | Decision | 2
f pvr_result | Result | choice | * [Verified; Not verified; Nonconformance raised]
f pvr_ncr | Nonconformance | record | when=pvr_result=Nonconformance_raised reqwhen=pvr_result=Nonconformance_raised
rule pvr_result | equals | Not verified | #FDE7E9 | bold
use pv_signatures
end

template process-verification-plan | Process Verification Plan | CONFIGURATION
packs aerospace
tags process verification, special process, qualification
purpose Plan how each process is verified or qualified: the specification, the method, the frequency, the qualified operators and equipment, and the evidence kept.
scope Processes the organization or its customers require to be verified or qualified, including special processes.
instructions List each process with its verification method and frequency. Requalification due dates in the past are highlighted.
workflow Drafted, approved by quality, reviewed when processes, specifications or equipment change.
retention Keep while current and for the retention period of the verification records.
section pvp_scope | Plan | 3
f pvp_site | Site | site | *
f pvp_owner | Plan owner | user | *
f pvp_as_of | As of | date | *
section pvp_items | Processes | 1
landscape-section
table pvp_rows | Processes | 1
c pq_process | Process | text | *
c pq_spec | Specification | text | *
c pq_method | Verification method | choice | * [Test pieces; Parameter monitoring; Destructive test; Non-destructive test; First article; Customer approval]
c pq_frequency | Frequency | text | *
c pq_customer_approved | Customer approval required | boolean
c pq_requal_due | Requalification due | date
c pq_status | Status | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(DAYS(pq_requal_due, pvp_as_of)), IF(DAYS(pq_requal_due, pvp_as_of) < 0, "Overdue", "Current"), "")}
rule pvp_rows.pq_status | equals | Overdue | #FDE7E9 | bold
f pvp_overdue | Requalifications overdue | calc | {COUNTIF(pvp_rows.pq_status, "Overdue")}
sign pvp_prepared | Prepared by | prepared | I prepared this process verification plan.
sign pvp_approved | Quality approval | approved | I approve this process verification plan. | inspection.approve
end
